# Repo-root ignores.
#
# frontend/ and backend/ carry their own .gitignore for their build output; this
# file covers the repo root, which had none. That gap is why a handful of
# zero-byte files created by mistyped shell redirects (`req.body`, `null)`,
# `frontend/console.log('DB` and friends) ended up committed.

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Secrets — belt and braces. The sub-app ignores already cover these, but a
# stray .env at the root would otherwise be committed with nothing to catch it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build output
dist/
build/
.next/
out/

# Local repo dumps and backups (large, regenerable, not source)
*.bundle
git-history.txt
git-timeline.txt

# Logs and caches
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.cache/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Editor and OS droppings
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
*.bak
*.orig

# Shell-redirect accidents: files whose names are fragments of code. These are
# always mistakes, never source.
`*`
*\)
*\(
